      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Concrete Implementations**\n\nI'm focusing on creating the `register_user.py` file to manage new user accounts. Firebase Authentication seems like a solid, well-documented choice for the external provider. I'm exploring its implementation details now, aiming for a clean and identifiable structure within the code.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Function**\n\nI'm now creating the `register_user.py` file and have outlined the function. It takes email and password, then utilizes the Firebase Admin SDK. The initialization of the Firebase Admin SDK is critical, which typically relies on a service account key file. I'll include a placeholder for this file path for now to keep things moving. I'm importing `firebase_admin`, `credentials`, and `auth` to ensure the core functionality.\n\n\n**Developing the Basic Structure**\n\nI've crafted the foundational structure of `register_user.py`. It includes the placeholder for the service account key. Importing modules like `firebase_admin`, `credentials`, and `auth` is underway to ensure essential functionality. I'm focusing on the `auth.create_user` operation within a defined function for creating a new user account.\n\n\n",
